  "question": {
    "text": "A thin circular metal disc of the radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> is set rotating about a central axis normal to its plane. Upon raising in temperature gradually, the radius increases to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>507</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>. The percentage change in the rotational kinetic energy will be"
  },
